  "modelingNotes": [
    "Charlotte Convention Center (501 S College St, opened 1995, Thompson, Ventulett, Stainback & Associates; expanded 2021) — original procedural geometry, CC0-1.0. bun generators/clt-convention-center.ts",
    "Map frame: x east, y north, z up, metres; origin at the anchor on the ground. Anchor = centroid of the OSM outline way/239813217, 35.2221174, -80.8453989. Its walls run at 50° / 140°, so the catalog bearing is 50: model +y points up College Street (NE, toward MLK Blvd), +x toward Brevard Street; College is the -x face, Stonewall St (now Brooklyn Village Ave) the -y face.",
    "Identity, in order: a very large, low, cream precast block filling the whole block between College and Brevard; the glazed barrel-vault concourses that cross it (College to Brevard) and run up beside the LYNX tracks to MLK, meeting at a glass-domed rotunda over a raised hub; arched glass entrances at the vault ends under bold curved white hoods between precast pylons; the 2021 rounded glass corner at College/Stonewall and the bridge over Stonewall to the Westin.",
    "Evidence: - plan: OSM outline way/239813217 and its 55 building:parts (way/ 1352238822-884) plus the hub relation/18569997; USGS NAIP orthophoto (tools/usgs.py naip, fetched Oct 2026) for the vaults, rotunda, roof ridges and the Stonewall bridge, which OSM does not map. - heights: lidar USGS_LPC_NC_Phase4_Mecklenburg_2016 (flown 2016-17), 1 m grid. Base = ground_min + 4.7 m (the Stonewall/Brevard corner, the lowest ground under the footprint); ground rises ~9.5 m to MLK and ~7 m to College (plane fit, used only to start facade detail above grade). Measured above base: hall roof 19.7, College wall 22.4, cross ridges 22.2-23, clerestory band 25.2, trench vent towers 28.1, concourse eaves ~23 under 25.6-26 crowns, hub 30.3, rotunda dome 39.2, spine 21 under ~24, ballroom 19.7 / 24.2 / 25.8 cross, MLK portal 21.3, court canopy 11. OSM part heights agree with these within ~1 m. - 2021 work (after the flight): the Stonewall-side meeting rooms take OSM's heights (19-23 m; the 2016 lidar shows ~11 m there); the rounded corner follows OSM's arc (fitted: centre -110.5/-72.5, radius 20 m, a quarter circle), glass from the plinth to 20.2 m under a 1.6 m cornice, in two-storey bands, height and teal-green glass (window-2 #55807c) from Mapillary 2022 image 180334787811096; the bridge's position and width (7 m) are measured on NAIP, its deck (7.5-13 m) is estimated. - published: opened 1995, TVS architects, 280,000 sq ft exhibit space, LYNX passes through it, $110M expansion with the Westin bridge completed Oct 2021 (Wikipedia, \"Charlotte Convention Center\"). - colour: precast panels cream-beige in every daylight photo (sunlit ~#e6dcc8, shade ~#cfc3ad) -> ccc-precast #e9dcc6; white membrane roofs on NAIP, pulled to a light grey (#c6cacc) so the vaults read; dark glazing = window; vaults and dome glass; hoods white = trim.",
    "Photos (evidence): - \"Charlotte Convention Center in 2017.jpg\", Kenneth C. Zirkel, CC BY-SA 4.0, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlotte_Convention_Center_in_2017.jpg (MLK entrance: hood, arched glass, pylons) - \"Entrance to Charlotte, NC, Convention Center IMG 5243.JPG\", Billy Hathorn, CC BY-SA 3.0, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_to_Charlotte,_NC,_Convention_Center_IMG_5243.JPG - \"Charlotte NC Convention Center 2007.jpg\", Kenneth C. Zirkel, CC BY-SA 4.0, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlotte_NC_Convention_Center_2007.jpg (College entrance and pylon) - \"Charlotte Convention Center\", pasa47, CC BY 2.0, https://www.flickr.com/photos/53301297@N00/49721488483 (MLK side, tracks) - \"Charlotte Skyline From the Caldwell Street South Blvd bridge.jpg\", John Ashley, CC BY 2.0, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlotte_Skyline_From_the_Caldwell_Street_South_Blvd_bridge.jpg (the long low mass from the south) - \"3rd Street (LYNX station).jpg\", Patriarca12, CC BY-SA 3.0, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:3rd_Street_(LYNX_station).jpg (the spine's vault beside the tracks) - Mapillary (CC BY-SA 4.0), contributors' images 180334787811096 (rounded corner, 2022), 501434965148436 (Stonewall face), 1063116400872692 (MLK face), 527573339047805 (College St), 1121186182150504 and 485654926906582 (Brevard). Look-only: none used. No commercial imagery.",
    "Estimated: window and bay sizes (photos, no dimensions), pylon sizes, hood depth (8 m at the crown) and fascia, the College face's clerestory windows, the court's glass wall height. Invented: the hood's plan curve law.",
    "Doubts: no licensed photo shows the 2021 Stonewall facade squarely or the Brevard entrance, so both are drawn like the 1995 faces; the College St face between the entrance and the corner is mostly hidden by trees in every photo. The \"spires\" in the brief's note were not found: the 2016 lidar has nothing above the 39 m dome, and the College St photos show pylons and a lattice sign frame, not towers; the arched entrances under their hoods are the curved glass features modelled.",
    "Left out: lettering, the lattice sign frames, mullions, rooftop plant.",
    "Original procedural model from https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks (catalog id \"clt-convention-center\", model \"clt-convention-center\"), generated by https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks/blob/a1974bbf738c6994edbe99a7a61818b9d69da9e0/generators/clt-convention-center.ts. That repository is the editable source; source.blend.gz is the exported mesh imported into Blender for convenience.",
    "Exported for Open Landmarks v1: placement bearing and scale baked in; moving parts frozen in their rest pose; footings and basements below the lowest ground (y = 0) cut away; material colours carried over exactly, as library finishes where they are not standard swatches.",
    "Window panels clipped to the walls behind them; 526 m² of glazing with no wall behind it (curtain walls, glazing past a wall's edge) uses the clt-convention-center-glazing finish in the window colour.",
    "To fit six materials, folded trim into clt-convention-center-ccc-precast (ΔE 7.5)."
